    "result_text": "The full suite (`BUILD SUCCESS`, all tests green) passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the disposable-domain email blocklist for owner creation (`POST /api/owners`), following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions.\n\nThe rule slots into the existing email handling in the create pipeline \u2014 right after `NormalizeEmail` (which trims/lower-cases the address), so the domain check judges the canonical form. Each piece landed in its natural home rather than being bolted onto an existing class:\n\n- **`util/DisposableEmailDomains.java`** \u2014 a pinned reference table (the blocklist: `mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`) with a case-insensitive `isBlocked(domain)` lookup, mirroring the existing `CityRegion`/`RegionPostcodes` utilities.\n- **`EmailNormalizer.domainOf(...)`** \u2014 a small domain-extraction helper added to the shared email utility, reused by the new step instead of duplicating parsing.\n- **`function/owner/ValidateEmailDomain.java`** \u2014 a single-responsibility pipeline step that skips absent/blank emails (email stays optional) and throws for a blocked domain.\n- **`escalation/DisposableEmailDomainException.java`** + **handler** + **escalation YAML** \u2014 a checked exception mapped to a 400, distinct from the existing `InvalidEmailException` syntax rejection.\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired `validateEmailDomain` between `normalizeEmail` and `build`.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.errorRejectsDisposableDomain` (posting `x@mailinator.com`) now returns 400, and the whole suite is green.",
